{"_id":"69a867a9a9c77b00e95e4929","referenceId":"eb0349d9-351b-4481-83db-ab4a638a84c9","type":"code","extension":"@cognigy/basic-nodes","label":"Knowledge","comment":"","commentColor":"","analyticsLabel":null,"isEntryPoint":false,"isDisabled":false,"mock":{"isEnabled":false,"code":""},"localizedData":[{"config":{"code":"context.knowledge = `\n##SimpliSafe Internal IT Help Desk Knowledge\n\nQ: How do I open an internal IT ticket?\nA: The fastest way is the IT portal. Choose the category that matches your issue—Access, Email & Collaboration, Hardware, or Software—then include a short summary, how urgent it is, and any screenshots you have. If you’re on a call, I can also create the ticket for you and read back the ticket number.\nLink (optional): https://it.simplisafe.example/portal/new\n\nQ: How do I check my ticket status or add more details after I submit it?\nA: You can track it in “My Requests.” Open the ticket and add comments or attachments. If you have new information—like the exact error text—add it there so the technician sees it immediately.\nLink (optional): https://it.simplisafe.example/portal/my-requests\n\nQ: What information should I provide so IT can resolve my issue faster?\nA: Please share: what you were trying to do, what happened, the exact wording of any error message, whether you’re blocked or just delayed, and whether it’s happening on one device or multiple. If you know your device name or asset tag, include that too. This helps us avoid back-and-forth questions.\nLink (optional): https://kb.simplisafe.example/it/ticket-template\n\nQ: I need access to an internal application—how do I request it?\nA: Submit an access request with the name of the app, the level of access you need, and why you need it for your role. If there’s an approver, add your manager or the app owner so it routes correctly. Access is granted using least privilege—only what you need to do your work.\nLink (optional): https://it.simplisafe.example/portal/access-request\n\nQ: How do I request membership changes for an email distribution list or group?\nA: Use the group request form and specify the group name, whether you need member or owner access, and who should approve it. If this is for a team change, include your department and start date so the request can be validated quickly.\nLink (optional): https://it.simplisafe.example/portal/groups\n\nQ: How do I request a shared mailbox?\nA: Request a shared mailbox when multiple people need to read and respond from a single address, like “team-support@.” You’ll need to name at least two owners, specify who needs “Send As” permissions, and confirm retention requirements if applicable.\nLink (optional): https://it.simplisafe.example/portal/shared-mailbox\n\nQ: How do I request a new distribution list (DL) or Teams-enabled group?\nA: Provide the purpose, naming convention, at least two owners, and whether membership should be open or restricted. We usually recommend restricted membership for operational groups to avoid accidental sprawl.\nLink (optional): https://it.simplisafe.example/portal/distribution-lists\n\nQ: How do I set up mailbox delegation (someone managing my calendar or inbox)?\nA: Delegation lets someone manage your calendar or mailbox without sharing your password. You can grant permissions like “Reviewer,” “Editor,” or “Delegate.” Start with the least access needed, and review it periodically.\nLink (optional): https://kb.simplisafe.example/m365/delegation\n\nQ: How do I share my calendar with my manager or teammate?\nA: You can share your calendar with specific people and set the level of detail they can see. For most cases, “Can view when I’m busy” is enough. If you share full details, keep confidential meetings marked private.\nLink (optional): https://kb.simplisafe.example/m365/calendar-sharing\n\nQ: How do I book conference rooms?\nA: Book rooms through your calendar by adding the room as a location. If you can’t see a room, it may not be in your building list or it may be restricted. If it’s missing, we can add you to the correct room list.\nLink (optional): https://kb.simplisafe.example/m365/rooms\n\nQ: I need a new software license (like Adobe, Jira, Figma). What’s the process?\nA: Submit a license request with the product name, your cost center, and why you need it. If it requires approval, include your manager. Once approved, IT assigns the license and confirms when it’s ready.\nLink (optional): https://it.simplisafe.example/portal/licenses\n\nQ: I need software that isn’t in the approved catalog. How do I request it?\nA: Submit a software review request with the vendor name, what data it will access, and the business reason. Security and compliance review it first. Once approved, IT will help deploy it or guide you through a safe installation.\nLink (optional): https://it.simplisafe.example/portal/software-review\n\nQ: How do I request onboarding for a new hire from the IT side?\nA: The hiring manager submits onboarding with the start date, role, location, and required tools. IT prepares accounts, access, and hardware based on standard role templates. If the hire needs special tools, include that in the request so approvals can happen before day one.\nLink (optional): https://it.simplisafe.example/portal/onboarding\n\nQ: How do I request offboarding for a departing employee?\nA: Submit offboarding as soon as a departure date is known. Include the last day, manager, and whether mailbox forwarding or an archive is needed. IT will disable access according to policy and coordinate device return.\nLink (optional): https://it.simplisafe.example/portal/offboarding\n\nQ: How do I change my display name or preferred name in company systems?\nA: Submit an identity/profile request. For legal name changes, follow HR’s documentation requirements. For preferred names, we can usually update the directory display name while keeping legal name records where required.\nLink (optional): https://it.simplisafe.example/portal/identity-profile\n\nQ: How do I request an email alias?\nA: Request the alias and explain why it’s needed—like supporting a project or team. IT will verify it follows naming standards and doesn’t conflict with existing mailboxes.\nLink (optional): https://it.simplisafe.example/portal/email-alias\n\nQ: How do I update my email signature?\nA: Use the approved signature template so branding and legal disclaimers are consistent. After you generate it, paste it into Outlook settings. If you need multiple signatures, create one for internal and one for external communication.\nLink (optional): https://tools.simplisafe.example/signature\n\nQ: I deleted an email or calendar item—can it be restored?\nA: First check Deleted Items and Recover Deleted Items if available. If it’s beyond self-recovery, IT may be able to restore within retention limits. Provide the approximate date, subject, and sender/recipient to help narrow the search.\nLink (optional): https://kb.simplisafe.example/m365/recover-email\n\nQ: How do I request creation of a new SharePoint site or Team?\nA: Submit a site request with at least two owners, the purpose, who needs access, and the sensitivity classification. We’ll ensure naming and retention policies are applied at creation time.\nLink (optional): https://it.simplisafe.example/portal/new-site\n\nQ: How do I securely share files with external partners?\nA: Use approved sharing methods and share only the minimum required. Avoid sending sensitive files by email attachment if a secure share is available. If policy blocks sharing, you can request a time-bound exception with a business justification.\nLink (optional): https://kb.simplisafe.example/share/share-externally\n\nQ: How do I request a password manager team vault?\nA: Request a vault when a team needs shared credentials or secrets. You’ll need vault owners, members, and the purpose. Store credentials in the vault—never in documents or chat messages.\nLink (optional): https://it.simplisafe.example/portal/password-vault\n\nQ: How do I report phishing or a suspicious message?\nA: Don’t click anything. Report it using the phishing report option in Outlook. If you already entered credentials, change your password immediately and report it as a security incident so we can check for suspicious sign-ins.\nLink (optional): https://security.simplisafe.example/report/phishing\n\nQ: How do I request a security exception (temporary or special-case access)?\nA: Submit an exception request with what you need, why, the duration, and how you’ll reduce risk. Security may ask for compensating controls like MFA, restricted IP ranges, or time-limited access.\nLink (optional): https://security.simplisafe.example/requests/exception\n\nQ: I need guest Wi-Fi for visitors for a meeting or event. What do I do?\nA: Submit a guest access request with the date, time, location, sponsor, and expected headcount. IT will provide instructions or a time-limited access method based on office policy.\nLink (optional): https://it.simplisafe.example/portal/guest-access\n\nQ: My badge doesn’t work or I need building access updated—who handles this?\nA: Building/badge access is handled by Facilities or Security, not Internal IT. Submit a facilities access request with your building and the access level needed. If your badge is lost, report it immediately.\nLink (optional): https://facilities.simplisafe.example/access\n\nQ: I lost my badge—what are the immediate steps?\nA: Report the badge as lost so it can be disabled, then request a replacement. If you’re on-site and can’t enter, contact the front desk or building security for temporary access.\nLink (optional): https://facilities.simplisafe.example/lost-badge\n\nQ: How do I request a new phone extension or voicemail reset?\nA: Submit a telephony request with your current extension, desired change, and whether it’s urgent. For voicemail resets, confirm your identity and we can reset it according to policy.\nLink (optional): https://it.simplisafe.example/portal/telephony\n\nQ: What should I do during an internal outage (email/SSO/tools down)?\nA: First check the internal status page for updates. If there’s an active incident, follow the workaround guidance. If there’s no incident posted, report it with what you’re seeing, when it started, and whether coworkers are impacted.\nLink (optional): https://status.simplisafe.example/\n\n\n###MISROUTED EXTERNAL CALLS (CUSTOMER PRODUCT QUESTIONS) — REDIRECT ONLY\n(Use these so Internal IT doesn’t “support customers” by accident.)\n\nCustomer Product Support:\n- Help Center: https://support.simplisafe.com/\n- Contact Us (chat + phone): https://support.simplisafe.com/page/contact-us\n- Phone support (8am–midnight ET): 1-888-910-1458\n\nAlarm in progress / dispatch:\n- Monitoring Center (24/7): 1 (855) 693-4911\n\nBuying / pricing / “help deciding”:\n- Main site: https://simplisafe.com/\n- Help deciding (8am–midnight ET): 1-800-297-1605\n\nReturns:\n- Return Policy: https://support.simplisafe.com/articles/orders-warranty/simplisafe-return-policy/634479f54a42432bbd44f8c0\n\nCancel service:\n- Terms of Service: https://simplisafe.com/legal/terms-of-service\n- Cancellation phone: 1-800-548-9508\n\nMedia:\n- Press room: https://press.simplisafe.com/\n- press@simplisafe.com\n\nUK:\n- https://simplisafe.co.uk/contact-us\n- 0800-456-1789\n\nCareers:\n- https://careers.simplisafe.com/\n\nHandoff script:\n“Thanks for reaching out — you’ve reached SimpliSafe Internal IT, which supports employee devices and access.\nFor product help, please use https://support.simplisafe.com/page/contact-us or call 1-888-910-1458 (8am–midnight ET).\nIf this is an alarm-in-progress emergency, call the Monitoring Center 24/7 at 1 (855) 693-4911.”\n`;\n\ncontext.software = `\nInternal (employee-facing)\n1. IT Service Portal / ITSM: https://it.simplisafe.example/portal\n2. Access Requests: https://it.simplisafe.example/portal/access-request\n3. Group/DL Requests: https://it.simplisafe.example/portal/groups\n4. Shared Mailboxes: 